         plugin that implements this interface and is rebuilt). AbstractionsContract.Version — the gate
         PluginLoadPolicy enforces — stays 1, so no installed plugin is refused. On balance a removal that no shipped
         binary can observe; the package version follows suit as a minor. -->
    <!-- 1.46.0 (AC-604): added the project-ownership seam — ICockpitHost.ClaimProjectOwnership/GetProjectFieldOwnership
         (both default-implemented: no-op / null) plus HostProjectField, ProjectFieldOwnership and
         ProjectOwnershipRegistration (new types) — a plugin that shares a project's definition elsewhere (AC-242's
         Depot sync) can claim Name/Description/Logo/Behaviour/McpOverlay/WorktreeSwitch as externally managed, with
         a project-wide default overridable per field, so the editor draws a ◆ Shared / ● This machine origin badge
         instead of treating every project the same. A project nothing ever claims resolves null and the editor is
         unchanged (acceptance criterion 4). Additions only — a minor; major and abstractionsVersion stay 1. No
         in-repo plugin calls this yet, so no minHostVersion bump accompanies it. -->
    <!-- 1.47.0 (AC-609): added to IPluginTranscriptReader a statusFile-carrying ReadActivityAsync overload and
         ReadEntries (with PluginTranscriptEntry / PluginTranscriptEntryKind / PluginTranscriptSlice) — both
         default-implemented, the first forwarding to the existing overload and the second reporting nothing, so an
         already-compiled plugin keeps its behaviour exactly. The overload exists because the older one has no way to
         know which transcript is the session's: all it is given is what was on disk before the launch, so it must
         take whichever artifact appears next — a race against every other invocation of the same CLI on the machine,
         and one whose loss is silent and permanent (the reader tails a foreign file that then stops growing, so the
         host is handed no activity at all and reports the session Idle for its whole life). A provider that can name
         its own transcript — the CLI states it in the statusline snapshot the host already polls — now does.
         ReadEntries is the same identity used for reading back: a TTY session's on-disk record is the only
         transcript it has, so this is what lets a read surface answer for one instead of denying it exists.
         Additions only — a minor; major and abstractionsVersion stay 1. -->
    <!-- 1.48.0 (AC-245): added the shared-project catalog seam — ICockpitHost.AddSharedProjectSource/
         RemoveSharedProjectSource/SharedProjectSources (all default-implemented: no-op / no-op / empty) plus
         ISharedProjectSource, SharedProject and SharedProjectListResult (new types) — a plugin that shares project
         definitions elsewhere (AC-242's Depot sync) can list the ones this machine has not bound to a local Project
         yet, so the Projects workspace can offer them beside the local ones. Additions only — a minor; major and
         abstractionsVersion stay 1. Consumed in-repo by Cockpit.Plugin.Depot, whose minHostVersion moves with it.
         Renumbered from a collision with 1.47.0 (AC-609) at merge time; no released version ever carried this
         entry as 1.47.0. -->
    <!-- 1.49.0 (AC-246): added ISharedProjectSource.PrepareBindingAsync — required, not default-implemented, since
         it is a member a plugin implements rather than one the host calls (the same "an interface the plugin
         implements is worse for an older binary, not better" reasoning 0.7.0's IPluginSettingsSections entry above
         already documents) — plus SharedProjectBinding/SharedProjectBindingResource/SharedProjectBindingResult (new
         types). Reads enough of a shared project's own portable definition (Name, Description, GitUrl,
         BehaviorPrompt, the worktree switch, the MCP overlay's enabled names, and its resource rows) for the host to
         build a usable local Project at the "Finish setting up…" bind step, without the App layer ever depending on
         a plugin's own on-disk shape (Depot's CockpitProjectDefinition never crosses this boundary). Major and
         abstractionsVersion stay 1. Consumed in-repo by Cockpit.Plugin.Depot, whose minHostVersion moves with it.
         Renumbered from a collision with 1.48.0 at merge time. -->
    <!-- 1.50.0 (AC-629): added SessionProviderRegistration.IsLoggedIn — the SDK mirror of a gate that lived on
         TtyProviderRegistration alone, so a provider registering only a session provider (Gemini, GitHub Models,
         Kimi) could declare none and every profile under it read as ready. Init-only with a null default: an
         already-compiled plugin reports no gate, still read as "manages its own auth". Implementers: the host
